      "id": "0ace7a8c-f966-4567-845f-d2911ef916b7",
      "name": "Write link to sheet"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Fill one PDF for every spreadsheet row\n\nA PDF mail merge: each row in your Google Sheet becomes its own filled PDF, saved to Google Drive, with the link written back to the row.\n\n**Before the first run**\n1. Open your blank PDF once at [justfill.app](https://justfill.app), check the fields and give them names that match your column headers (for example `Name`, `Start date`). Save it as a template.\n2. Create a JustFill API key under Account, API keys.\n3. Add a column called `PDF link` to the sheet.\n\nFree accounts get watermarked PDFs. Paid plans produce clean files.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "762c3df0-94c8-42be-ad09-c8a001b57d1e",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Settings\n\nPaste your JustFill API key and a public link to the same blank PDF you saved as a template. `fileNameColumn` picks the column used to name each file.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "f9ce5a1f-6bf7-4ae3-b04f-120f693b4ed2",
      "name": "Sticky Note Step 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Read the sheet and open the PDF\n\nAll rows are read, then the PDF is opened **once**. Because it matches your saved template, the field names come back straight away with no detection step.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        420,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "ac77350b-f693-46af-b8fb-a7b2af52eec1",
      "name": "Sticky Note Step 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Match columns to fields\n\nColumn headers are matched to field names, ignoring case, spaces and punctuation. Columns without a matching field are skipped and listed in `unmatchedColumns`. Empty rows are skipped.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "a45444c0-3975-4c3f-a476-6407b929e510",
      "name": "Sticky Note Step 3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Fill, save and link each row\n\nOne row at a time: JustFill fills the PDF, the file is downloaded right away (the next fill replaces the link), uploaded to Google Drive and its link is written to the `PDF link` column of that row.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 1060,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1500,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "e719398b-ead9-499e-815c-ce5964d2658e",
      "name": "Sticky Note Step 4"
    }
  ],
